A git graph visualizes a repository's branch and commit history, showing branch creations, commits, merges, and tags. Use it for documenting release workflows, explaining branching strategies, and illustrating code review processes. Uses `gitGraph`.

---

!! Basic example

```
gitGraph
    commit id: "Initial commit"
    branch feature
    checkout feature
    commit id: "Add feature"
    checkout main
    merge feature
    commit id: "Release v1.0"
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
