$$$

---

!! Real-world example: GitFlow release workflow

This example shows a GitFlow-style release cycle with main, develop, feature branches, a release branch, and a hotfix. Branch colors follow the Mermaid default `git0`–`git7` palette order.

```
gitGraph
    accTitle: GitFlow release workflow
    accDescr: Feature development, release preparation, and hotfix cycle

    %% ── Initial setup ───────────────────────────
    commit id: "Project init" tag: "v0.0.1"

    %% ── Feature development ─────────────────────
    branch develop
    checkout develop
    commit id: "Setup CI"

    branch feature/user-auth
    checkout feature/user-auth
    commit id: "Add login form"
    commit id: "Add JWT handler"
    commit id: "Add refresh token"

    %% ── Merge feature back ───────────────────────
    checkout develop
    merge feature/user-auth id: "Merge user-auth"
    commit id: "Integration tests"

    branch feature/dashboard
    checkout feature/dashboard
    commit id: "Dashboard skeleton"
    commit id: "Add charts"

    checkout develop
    merge feature/dashboard id: "Merge dashboard"

    %% ── Release preparation ──────────────────────
    branch release/1.0
    checkout release/1.0
    commit id: "Bump version to 1.0"
    commit id: "Update changelog"

    checkout main
    merge release/1.0 id: "Release 1.0" tag: "v1.0.0"
    checkout develop
    merge release/1.0 id: "Back-merge 1.0"

    %% ── Hotfix ───────────────────────────────────
    checkout main
    branch hotfix/auth-crash
    checkout hotfix/auth-crash
    commit id: "Fix null pointer in JWT"
    commit id: "Add regression test"

    checkout main
    merge hotfix/auth-crash id: "Hotfix 1.0.1" tag: "v1.0.1"
    checkout develop
    merge hotfix/auth-crash id: "Back-merge hotfix"
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
